WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.083
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:08.909
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:14.775
Unit thirty-nine: Review: A2 Grammar. Today you will review the main grammar of A2.

4
00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:17.809
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:21.976
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:23.992
Past simple.

7
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:27.923
Past simple means the tense for finished actions.

8
00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:29.622
I went home.

9
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:32.683
Your turn. Say: Past simple.

10
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:37.127
Past simple.

11
00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:39.256
Present continuous.

12
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.480
Present continuous means the tense for actions happening now.

13
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.293
I am studying.

14
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:49.116
Your turn. Say: Present continuous.

15
00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:53.386
Present continuous.

16
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.116
Going to.

17
00:00:56.117 --> 00:00:58.093
Going to means the form for plans.

18
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:00.149
I am going to travel.

19
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.251
Your turn. Say: Going to.

20
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.089
Going to.

21
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.141
Comparatives.

22
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:13.148
Comparatives means forms that compare two things.

23
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.947
Bigger and better are comparatives.

24
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.075
Your turn. Say: Comparatives.

25
00:01:21.933 --> 00:01:23.236
Comparatives.

26
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.286
Present perfect.

27
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:30.024
Present perfect means the tense for experiences and recent results.

28
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:32.221
I have visited Paris.

29
00:01:32.817 --> 00:01:35.655
Your turn. Say: Present perfect.

30
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:39.675
Present perfect.

31
00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:41.441
Modals.

32
00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.216
Modals means verbs like can, must and should.

33
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:47.561
Modals take the base verb.

34
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.442
Your turn. Say: Modals.

35
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.266
Modals.

36
00:01:55.017 --> 00:01:56.006
Conditional.

37
00:01:57.017 --> 00:01:59.028
Conditional means a sentence with if.

38
00:01:59.617 --> 00:02:01.280
If it rains, we stay.

39
00:02:01.883 --> 00:02:04.327
Your turn. Say: Conditional.

40
00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:08.156
Conditional.

41
00:02:08.917 --> 00:02:09.895
Review.

42
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:13.185
Review means a look back at what you learned.

43
00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:15.272
Let's review the unit.

44
00:02:15.883 --> 00:02:18.547
Your turn. Say: Review.

45
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.401
Review.

46
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.735
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:31.582
Visal, this is the last lesson of A2. What can you now say?

48
00:02:32.683 --> 00:02:41.942
I can use the past simple and the present continuous. I can talk about plans with going to and about experiences with the present perfect.

49
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.746
Which new structures did we learn in the second half?

50
00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:59.139
First conditional, relative clauses, the passive, reported speech, phrasal verbs, time clauses, be able to and linking words. We also practised for and since.

51
00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.226
How can you continue to improve?

52
00:03:03.317 --> 00:03:16.757
Read short texts, write a few sentences every day, and speak with friends. Check your tenses and your word order. Now you are ready for B1, where the structures become more flexible.

53
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.505
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:23.127
Grammar focus: A2 grammar review.

55
00:03:23.427 --> 00:03:24.637
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.071
I went to the market yesterday.

57
00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:29.936
She has visited Siem Reap twice.

58
00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.791
If it rains, we will stay at home.

59
00:03:33.733 --> 00:03:42.632
Check the tense, the verb form and the word order. Remember the past simple, present continuous, going to, comparatives, present perfect, modals and conditionals.

60
00:03:43.383 --> 00:03:46.709
Be careful! Don't say: I have seen him yesterday.

61
00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.759
Say: I saw him yesterday.

62
00:03:51.059 --> 00:03:53.047
Use past simple with yesterday.

63
00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.404
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.677
Looking Back at A2.

65
00:03:58.977 --> 00:04:02.753
In A2 we studied the past simple and the present continuous.

66
00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:07.473
We learned going to, comparatives, modals and the present perfect.

67
00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:11.778
We also used conditionals, relative clauses and the passive.

68
00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:16.484
Reported speech and phrasal verbs gave us more natural English.

69
00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.301
With practice, B1 will be a smooth next step.

70
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.367
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:26.217 --> 00:04:28.181
I blank to the market yesterday.

72
00:04:28.481 --> 00:04:31.705
A, go. B, went. C, have gone.

73
00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.371
The answer is B: went.

74
00:04:38.517 --> 00:04:40.319
She blank studying right now.

75
00:04:40.619 --> 00:04:43.634
A, is. B, are. C, was.

76
00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.596
The answer is A: is.

77
00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.494
If it rains, we blank at home.

78
00:04:51.794 --> 00:04:55.366
A, stay. B, will stay. C, stayed.

79
00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.760
The answer is B: will stay.

80
00:05:01.917 --> 00:05:03.580
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:09.274
A, I have seen him yesterday.. B, I saw him yesterday.. C, I see him yesterday..

82
00:05:12.833 --> 00:05:15.704
The answer is B: I saw him yesterday..

83
00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:20.208
According to the reading, what will be a smooth next step?

84
00:05:20.508 --> 00:05:24.544
A, B1. B, silence. C, a long holiday.

85
00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.960
The answer is A: B1.

86
00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:34.434
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:35.283 --> 00:05:38.142
Which A2 grammar point do you want to practise more?

88
00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.404
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:48.704 --> 00:06:03.619
I want to practise the present perfect more, because it is difficult for me to choose between it and the past simple. I will read short texts and write sentences about my experiences. Then I will feel more confident.

90
00:06:03.919 --> 00:06:05.535
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:10.821
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and a2 grammar review.

92
00:06:11.121 --> 00:06:16.632
Today's value is growth mindset. Mistakes help you grow. Keep learning, step by step.

93
00:06:16.932 --> 00:06:23.801
Congratulations! You have finished Online Grammar, level A two. See you in Online Grammar, level B one!

94
00:06:24.101 --> 00:06:26.602
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

